  "_adamantyl_stereo_is_VACUOUS": "The printed names decorate the cage as (3r,5r,7r)- or (3R,5R,7R)-adamantan-1-yl. RDKit finds ONE stereocentre in every product, the glycerol C2. Adamantane's bridgeheads are not stereogenic, so those descriptors constrain nothing and the stereo assertion above says nothing about them -- it is vacuous there, not passing. The paper itself writes them lower-case 'r' in some entries and upper-case 'R' in others, which is the same point.",
